Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Depth snapshot residency diagnostics (memory spike,
 FIX-PLAN step 0; draft)

Counts depth feedback snapshots that are created and not yet disposed (their last
command buffer has not completed) with the snapshot root's allocated size, and
how long each stayed resident. The native timing summary gains
depth_snapshot_residency: resident count and bytes now, peak bytes and longest
residency since the previous summary, retired count and summed residency
(cumulative). Counts only: allocation, encoding and drawing are unchanged; a
failure to read the size counts 0 bytes and never stops the draw.

Compile-checked (compile-check.sh, offline packages). Not built into an app,
not run, not reviewed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
